This code uses the memoized dynamic programming approach with bottom-up traversal. The `memo` decorator `@functools.lru_cache((m, n), 1)` memoizes the results of the subproblems. In each subproblem, when visiting a cell containing grass, its adjacent cells are also visited recursively until we find all adjacent cells that are still unvisited and have grass in them (these will be marked). This guarantees that during each recursive call on a cell with grass, all surrounding grass is already cut. The minimum number of moves is achieved by considering the cell with the most grass as the cutting row/column in each step. Finally, in `main()`, the provided test cases are inputted and the function `solve()` is called for each case to output the answer.

